[[2207,844,"over a number of years the amount of prescribed opiates had increased to a level where they led her to fall asleep and fall over","high dose prescribed opiates",""],[11056,4252,"gloves were in open and easily accessible locations throughout the home including in rooms and the kitchen area","gloves accessible to residents",""],[11057,4252,"earlier incident when Christine Neild had put non- food items in her mouth","non-food items placed in mouth",""],[11058,4252,"no regular use of sensors to alert night staff of a resident getting up and wandering","absence of sensor alerts",""],[11233,4309,"The inquest heard that Mr Townsend should have seen a GP and had further tests prior to his admission to Salford Royal Hospital. The inquest heard that at the GP practice in question there were insufficient GPs to see patients. In addition there was no evidence of a clear escalation process from the Nurse to a Doctor within the practice.","insufficient GPs to see patients",""],[11234,4309,"The particular risks he presented with his background health issues were not recognised when he showed signs of being unwell","unrecognised risks due to background health issues",""],[11235,4309,"The quality of the written medical notes at the GP practice was poor","poor quality written medical notes",""],[11236,4309,"The inquest heard that there had been concerns locally within the area about the GP practice. They were now being acted upon by the CCG but the situation had been an issue for some time before there was intervention","local concerns about GP practice",""],[11904,4589,"The inquest heard that when Mr Reid went to see his GP she was very concerned about the risk he posed to himself and wanted him to be seen urgently by the Home Based Treatment Team (HBTT). The initial call was to the Manchester team -because the GP practice was within the City Of Manchester-who accept referrals from GPs.","lack of urgent mental health assessment for residents",""],[15061,5882,"no guidelines in place to reduce the quantity of drugs available to Mr Robb at any one time","uncontrolled medication quantity",""],[15062,5882,"limited evidence of information sharing between the members of the Trafford Adult Safeguarding Board","information sharing failure",""],[15063,5882,"only 1 strategic meeting took place over a 6 year period","insufficient strategic meetings",""]]